+
+| Term | Definition |
+|---|---|
+| critical print size | 0.2° of x-height: the smallest print read at full speed; speed holds to 2° (Legge & Bigelow 2011) |
+| farthest reader | a phone held 58 cm away to read a message (Bababekova et al. 2011: 17.5–58 cm, mean 36.2, 129 people) |
+| CSS pixel on a phone | 0.160 mm [ASSUMED: a 6.3-inch 1080 × 2400 screen, 416 ppi, device pixel ratio 2.625] |
+| the box's x-height | 580 mm × tan 0.2° ÷ 0.160 mm = 12.65 px; at x 0.46 em, type of 27.5 px, or the page's when larger (SillyTavern's own x of 8.2 px reaches 0.2° only to 38 cm) |
+| the box's lines | boxLines × the box's size ÷ the page's: 4 at 17.85 px → 6 at 27.5, so a box holds the letters it held |
+| the scene line | place · story time · light (the engine's place, clock and sky), each left out when unknown: what a visual novel's background tells |
+
+| IF | THEN |
+|---|---|
+| the box shows a unit | its type is the box's size; the device's send time is hidden; the scene line stands above the chat |
+| a scroll reaches the box's end | it stays in the box (overscroll-behavior: contain), so a pull at a phone's top does not reload the page |
+| the screen is short (a phone held sideways) | the box stops at 60 % of the height and its lines scroll |
