 **The music (2026-11-11 (118); `rules/music.ts`, `rules/data/feeling-va.ts`, `index.ts` musicNow, playSong, addSongs and drawSongs; the setting "Music", on by default, silent until songs are added).** The player's songs are placed by measurement, as a vowel by its formants, and the song nearest the scene's feelings plays. Voice and music carry emotion in one code: across 104 studies of voices and 41 of music performance the same acoustic changes convey the same emotion (Juslin & Laukka 2003), faster, louder and brighter going with higher activation; mode leads listeners' judgements of happy against sad, then tempo, register, dynamics, articulation and timbre, each adding to the others (Eerola, Friberg & Bresin 2013). The player's picks (2026-11-11): the characters' recorded feelings set the target; songs are measured in the browser as they are added; named sets first, measured areas otherwise.
